Chapter: PlugBuildScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter Pipeline
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

 THE TWENTY-THIRD GENERATOR ON THE PIPELINE MODEL (PipelineModel.md), and the
 SMALLEST in the tree. The emitted script is byte-identical to the one that
 shipped before the migration.

 `-Force` IS DECLARED AND USED NOWHERE, the second parameter of that shape
 after `sweep-apps`' `-Jobs`. Verified at head twice: `Force` appears exactly
 once in `build/plug-build.ps1`, on its parameter line, and the builder it
 calls has no such parameter to forward it to (the only `Force` in
 `codex/plugs/common/plug-build-lib.ps1` is an unrelated `New-Item -Force` at
 line 200). So a caller passing `-Force` expecting a rebuild gets an ordinary
 one, and no wiring exists that could ever carry the switch. Recorded rather
 than repaired here: deleting a parameter changes the emitted bytes and this
 migration's gate is byte-identity (L-ACCEPTED).

Section: Parameters

  plugbuild-params : List ShellParam = [sh-param "PlugName" SptString, sh-param "Chapters" SptStringArray, sh-param-optional "Force" SptSwitch]

Section: The pipeline, declared before it is spelled

  plug-dir-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "plugDir", pa-kind = PkDir, pa-expr = SeVar "plugDir", pa-from = Just (SeRaw "Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..' 'codex' 'plugs' $PlugName") }

  pb-arts : List PipeArtifact = [plug-dir-art]

Section: S01 -- Script Header

  s01-body : List ShellCmd = [ScComment "Build plugs/<PlugName>/build-output/<PlugName>-plug.cdx"]

  s01 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "header", ps-why = "name the artifact this script produces, which no later line states", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s01-body }

Section: S02 -- Preamble

  s02-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScSetStrictMode, ScSetErrorStop]

  s02 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "preamble", ps-why = "strict mode and stop on error", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s02-body }

Section: S03 -- Dot-source Library

  s03-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScRunDot (SeRaw "(Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..' 'codex' 'plugs' 'common' 'plug-build-lib.ps1')")]

  s03 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "load the plug library", ps-why = "Build-TranspilerPlug lives in the plugs' shared library, so every plug builds the same way", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s03-body }

Section: S04 -- Build Invocation

  s04-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, pipe-produce plug-dir-art, ScIf (SeNot (SeRaw "(Test-Path -PathType Container $plugDir)")) [ScWriteError (SeRaw "\"MISSING plug directory: $plugDir\""), ScExit (SeInt 2)] [], ScRaw "Build-TranspilerPlug -PlugDir $plugDir -PlugName $PlugName -Chapters $Chapters"]

 THE GUEST IS THE LIBRARY'S, NOT THIS SCRIPT'S: `Build-TranspilerPlug` compiles
 the chapters, so the resource is declared here because a caller of this script
 pays for it, even though no line below spells a boot.

  s04 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "build the plug", ps-why = "refuse a plug name that names no directory, then hand the chapters to the shared builder", ps-in = ["PlugName", "Chapters"], ps-out = [plug-dir-art], ps-needs = [PrGuests 1], ps-verdict = [PoExit 2 "the named plug has no directory under codex/plugs, so there is nothing to build"], ps-body = s04-body }

Section: Assembly

  pb-pipe : Pipeline = Pipeline { pl-name = "plug-build", pl-doc = "Build a transpiler plug CDX from name and chapter list", pl-params = plugbuild-params, pl-stages = [s01, s02, s03, s04] }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell (pipeline-to-shell pb-pipe))
  end

